    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d778">

                <pb facs="0731" n="633" xml:id="pg633"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Lord Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1924.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note, No. 265, of the 15th instant, by which you transmit an
                    expression of the great sorrow with which Her Majesty the Queen has learnt the
                    details of the terrible disaster at Galveston and the assurance of her sincere
                    sympathy with the unfortunate sufferers from this calamity.</p>
                <p>Your note has been communicated to the President, who charges me to express his
                    sincere appreciation of Her Majesty’s sympathetic message.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
